From aa76e16f77eeec0fde4494137666c3c3e8530742 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:06:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] overclock: CPU and GPU overclocking on the Raspberry Pi 5

An Overclocking category, shown on the RPi5 when pi-overclock is
installed: live clocks, temperature, fan and throttling; the Stock, Mild,
Moderate and High presets, and custom values in expert mode; Apply and
test, which restarts into a tryboot trial whose settings are kept only if
its stability test passes; an extended stability test with a progress
dialog; Revert to stock; and help on cooling, benefits and recovery.

Every operation runs pi-overclock --json; value lists come from its
limits, so the menu can't offer a value it would refuse. After a trial
or a boot-guard shutdown, the service reports the result.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
---
